1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
and

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
We'll be right back.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
We'll be right back.

4
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:59,980
We'll be right back.

5
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:05,800
But you were really looking forward to watching Kaze Haya play today, weren't you?

6
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:14,420
You see, hearing he played baseball in middle school, I made it my goal to witness it. It became important to me.

7
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:20,160
All I wanted was to see a side of Kaze Haya I didn't know yet.

8
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:25,720
Is that so? Are you saying that you actually know things about him then?

9
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:27,620
Cause I don't think you do.

10
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:32,520
Don't treat my feelings the same way as yours.

11
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:38,980
I've always watched Kaze Haya. It's something I've done ever since we were in middle school together.

12
00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:41,380
On rainy days.

13
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:41,980
Really?

14
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,760
On windy days.

15
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:44,620
No way!

16
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,080
Even on snowy days.

17
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,220
In the cold too?

18
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:55,520
So, then, whenever I would see him talking to other girls, I'd intervene and try to prevent him from dating any of them.

19
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:56,560
You...

20
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:59,260
You've worked so hard!

21
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:01,820
Oh, well, yeah! Of course I have!

22
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:04,760
Man, that was a close one.

23
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:10,020
But anyway, the point is, I can confidently say I know Kaze Haya quite well.

24
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:12,540
And it's not as if this is anything new either.

25
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:15,660
Like I was saying, I've watched over him forever.

26
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:22,080
You're out!

27
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,260
Let's keep this up!

28
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:25,440
Yeah!

29
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:29,560
It's impossible...

30
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,540
to keep your eyes off him.

31
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:39,400
Don't try to act like you understand how I feel.

32
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:45,780
Suddenly, Kaze Haya is right there in front of me.

33
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,540
And I can't look away.

34
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:52,860
Before I know it, I'm already thinking about him.

35
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:57,560
As I'm falling asleep, his face immediately comes to mind.

36
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:00,300
Everything is a first for me.

37
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:04,860
I thought this feeling I was experiencing was something special.

38
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:09,060
I'm very aware of the fact that I don't know that much about myself.

39
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,360
Or about Kaze Haya, either.

40
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:14,400
Would I still feel the same way I've been feeling lately

41
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,100
if it was someone other than him?

42
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:19,600
Perhaps there's something more beyond this I haven't been able to grasp yet.

43
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,820
I want to know.

44
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:28,320
To be honest, I want to learn more about him.

45
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:30,020
About my own feelings.

46
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,740
I have to know more.

47
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:34,040
Strike! And you're out!

48
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:37,540
I'll try talking to Sanada to understand him better.

49
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:42,060
I'm really grateful for all of your help.

50
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:45,500
Did she accept my challenge?

51
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:52,900
No matter what, I'm going to keep doing things my way until I get what I want.

52
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:58,880
Uh, but wait, the game isn't over yet.

53
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:00,080
Huh?

54
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:03,760
D-did she not want to sit here and watch it with me?

55
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:05,480
Ugh.

56
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:09,220
When it comes to Kurumi,

57
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:13,060
I can't even imagine how special Kaze Haya must be to her.

58
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:15,320
She's known him for so long.

59
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,780
I want him to be my boyfriend.

60
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:19,880
Boyfriend?

61
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:21,400
Oh, I see.

62
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:23,680
So are feelings for him are romantic.

63
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:27,960
Romantic feelings?

64
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,200
Romantic feelings.

65
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:43,520
I think this is the first time I've clearly recognized and processed those words.

66
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:47,940
Thanks a lot for the good game.

67
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:48,640
Yeah!

68
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:51,900
We actually won!

69
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:54,300
I'm so glad.

70
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:56,300
Congrats on the win, Kaze Haya.

71
00:05:58,680 --> 00:05:59,780
Congrats, everyone.

72
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:01,500
Oh, that's right.

73
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,320
Kurumi never did come back.

74
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:04,400
Oh, jeez.

75
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,620
You were here the whole time?

76
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:07,840
When your hairstyle's different,

77
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:09,400
it's pretty hard to know it's you.

78
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:10,820
Hi, Endo.

79
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:12,360
Call me Tomo.

80
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:15,100
Isn't it great?

81
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:15,920
We won!

82
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:16,560
Yeah.

83
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:19,180
We're going to cheer for the volleyball game next.

84
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:20,580
You should come with us.

85
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:21,400
What?

86
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:22,240
Can I?

87
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:23,340
You sure?

88
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:24,900
What are you talking about?

89
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,900
Weren't you planning to show your support for Ayana and Jizu?

90
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:29,260
Echo's playing too.

91
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:30,580
Come on.

92
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:31,600
Let's get going.

93
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:34,040
Oh, no.

94
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:35,460
I didn't say anything wrong.

95
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:36,060
Did I, Soliko?

96
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:37,640
No.

97
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:39,360
It's just...

98
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,400
I'm happy.

99
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,500
Thank you.

100
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,520
I'd love to.

101
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:46,340
Mm-hmm.

102
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:50,000
Being alone was normal for me until recently.

103
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,360
But now...

104
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:54,840
I have so many kind-hearted people in my life.

105
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:58,740
I'm sure if even one of them was missing,

106
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:01,220
things would have turned out much differently.

107
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:08,720
And of course, if Kazehaya wasn't around, then I never would have known that anyone could be this kind.

108
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,720
I'm so grateful for him.

109
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:10,980
I'm so grateful for him.

110
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:15,900
My world has changed drastically.

111
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:20,720
Admiration, respect, romantic feelings.

112
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:23,880
I don't know my own feelings.

113
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:25,740
But I want to learn.

114
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:28,540
I want to find out more about them.

115
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:31,640
It makes him the same as Kazehaya, doesn't it?

116
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:39,040
If I talk to Sanada, will I learn more?

117
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:41,700
Will I be able to find an answer?

118
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:50,960
Come on, let's get back.

119
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,300
Yeah, what's next?

120
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:54,860
I think it might be girls volleyball and boys soccer?

121
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:56,800
Hmm?

122
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:59,740
Hey, uh, so earlier.

123
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:00,560
Earlier?

124
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,600
Uh, uh, are you into Kuro Numa?

125
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:09,620
Ah, Sakako.

126
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:11,560
Or wait, no, Sawako?

127
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:12,920
Right?

128
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:15,260
Her name's Kuro Numa.

129
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:16,480
Kuro Numa?

130
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:17,360
Kuro!

131
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,560
Oh, so you mean like black.

132
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:27,020
I will admit that I actually like Kuriyama.

133
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:30,040
But none of the way you're probably thinking, Shota.

134
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:35,200
It's Kuro Numa.

135
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:35,980
Huh?

136
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:37,600
Is that not what I said?

137
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:39,780
You said Yama again.

138
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:40,220
Did I?

139
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:42,460
What?

140
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:43,700
This about that curveball?

141
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:45,300
No, just forget it.

142
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,120
I caught it because I was the closest.

143
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:51,220
Yeah, I know that.

144
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:54,120
I know, but...

145
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:59,300
My first thought after it happened was,

146
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:01,320
I wish I had caught it instead.

147
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:03,000
Hmm.

148
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:07,100
Looks like girls soccer and boys softball won their first matches.

149
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,860
That means free barbecue.

150
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:11,160
Mr. Peen.

151
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:11,620
Huh?

152
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:14,360
I'd like to check the field day committee members' schedule

153
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:15,820
if you wouldn't mind showing me.

154
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:16,740
Mm-hmm.

155
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:19,460
I need their year in class.

156
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:20,500
And their name.

157
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:22,380
Oh, um...

158
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:25,220
Actually, I'm pretty sure I can look that much up on my own.

159
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:26,380
What the...

160
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:27,000
No way!

161
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,260
Just tell me and I can give you the info.

162
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:31,720
I mean...

163
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:33,020
I would, but...

164
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:34,920
I really don't want to inconvenience you.

165
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:37,940
What is with this kid?

166
00:09:39,460 --> 00:09:39,900
Here.

167
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:41,720
I really appreciate it.

168
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:43,520
Kazehaya is...

169
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:46,520
There.

170
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:49,360
He's cleaning up equipment in the afternoon

171
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,420
and then carrying it to the storage room.

172
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:53,860
Once you're done with your business, get out of here.

173
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:54,820
Okay.

174
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:58,380
Thank you so much, Mr. Peen.

175
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:00,960
If you'll please excuse me.

176
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,400
Uh, sure.

177
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:06,880
What's with that over-excessive smiling?

178
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:07,960
It's creepy.

179
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:20,840
Without fail,

180
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:24,300
I have always watched over Kazehaya.

181
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:35,460
Now, which one should I get for Chizu?

182
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:36,640
Oh.

183
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:42,320
Oh.

184
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:44,540
If it isn't Miss Kurumi.

185
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:48,600
Uh, you're Aya and Ayano, isn't that right?

186
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:51,200
And I believe you're friends with Sawako and Chizu.

187
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,460
Uh-huh.

188
00:10:52,700 --> 00:10:54,880
I heard that you went to Chizu's middle school.

189
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:55,640
Mm-hmm.

190
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:59,860
Hey, uh, I'm curious.

191
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:01,500
What skin toner do you use?

192
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:03,400
I don't... use any.

193
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:04,680
Huh?

194
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,960
I'm using a face mask tonight.

195
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:10,020
My sister's expensive one.

196
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:13,940
I'm honestly surprised you knew my name.

197
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:15,080
Oh, right.

198
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:17,120
I guess there were all those rumors.

199
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:18,640
Rumors?

200
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:21,540
Don't worry about things like that.

201
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:23,680
People who spread gossip are just troubled.

202
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:25,300
That's true.

203
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:28,420
And the ones who believe them are stupid.

204
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:31,800
By the way, I'm assuming you heard the rumors, too.

205
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,740
Did you talk to anyone about them?

206
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:34,660
No way!

207
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,520
I never trusted any of that nonsense.

208
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:40,060
I just overheard it from a group of girls who were discussing it one day.

209
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:41,300
Oh, of course.

210
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:44,660
Can't imagine someone like you ever spreading gossip.

211
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:48,200
That's nice of you to say.

212
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:53,620
You know, I have this theory.

213
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:56,800
The rumors were spread by someone who likes Kaze Haya.

214
00:11:57,980 --> 00:12:00,680
I bet Sawako was in the way so the person felt threatened.

215
00:12:01,340 --> 00:12:05,100
And if me and Chizu were Sawako's backup, it'd be difficult to mess with her.

216
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:08,480
Plus, putting aside what was said about me,

217
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:12,820
a majority of Chizu's rumors were slightly exaggerated things that actually happened.

218
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:19,280
And knowing that is why I think it was someone who went to the same middle school as Chizu and Kaze Haya.

219
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:23,680
But I wonder what that girl's gonna do if Kaze Haya finds out about this.

220
00:12:26,860 --> 00:12:27,860
Who's to say?

221
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:32,440
Though, you can't accuse someone if there isn't any evidence.

222
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:36,940
So you can't.

223
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:42,240
Looks like we ended up talking for a while, huh?

224
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:44,480
We did.

225
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:47,380
The game's starting up soon, so I think I'll get going.

226
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:49,880
Well, I wish you luck with everything.

227
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:50,680
Yeah.

228
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,420
You too, Ayane.

229
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:53,900
Thanks, Sia.

230
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:57,600
Oh, by the way,

231
00:12:57,720 --> 00:13:01,040
she's surprisingly tough, isn't she?

232
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:03,420
Since she plays fair and square.

233
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,740
Wait, Kaze Haya has another game?

234
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:16,300
Yeah, you don't remember?

235
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:18,560
He's also got field day committee work.

236
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:20,560
Ryu, what are you gonna do after this?

237
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:22,780
Eating a nap, probably.

238
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:24,500
Really?

239
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:25,520
Lunch already?

240
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:27,520
And then a little siesta, huh?

241
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:29,480
Trash?

242
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,840
But my nap.

243
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:41,980
Uh, what's wrong?

244
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:42,480
You okay?

245
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:44,100
Oh, man.

246
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:46,140
Guess I can nap outside.

247
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:46,720
What?

248
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:47,480
Where at?

249
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:50,160
Maybe somewhere near the PE equipment room?

250
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,260
Uh, why in a place like that?

251
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:53,760
Who cares?

252
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,820
Let him sleep where he wants.

253
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:56,360
Tough?

254
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:57,760
Yeah, right.

255
00:13:58,160 --> 00:14:00,460
My calculations were a bit off, that's all.

256
00:14:04,860 --> 00:14:05,800
Good job, guys.

257
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:06,920
Thought you could use these.

258
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:08,680
Thanks, you read my mind, Sadako.

259
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,940
All right, now tell me, how did I do out there?

260
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:12,860
Oh, my gosh, you were amazing.

261
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,020
And very red.

262
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:15,080
Stop it.

263
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:16,120
You're making me blush.

264
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:18,480
Guess you got your money's worth out of that shirt.

265
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:19,460
What should we do?

266
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:20,240
Go get lunch?

267
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:21,020
Works for me.

268
00:14:21,380 --> 00:14:22,580
Are you feeling hungry, too?

269
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:23,320
Yeah!

270
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:27,360
Um, I have some business that I should probably take care of.

271
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:28,020
What kind?

272
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:33,440
A softball almost hit me during the game earlier, but Sanada saved me by catching it, so I wanted

273
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,440
to say thanks to him.

274
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:34,840
Yeah?

275
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,280
Ryu did that?

